IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nz-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `nz-part2-definitions`
IMPORT `nz-part2-commencement-repeal`
IMPORT `nz-schedules`

-- Tests for nz-schedules.l4 (Schedules 1 to 3).
-- Every expected value was decided by reading the clause quoted beside it BEFORE the module was run.
-- The main commencement date is a supplied input in every test (the Act does not date it): 1 January 2021 is used throughout, an invented value, as are the other dates below.

§ `Schedule 1 clause 2 -- Definitions for this Part`

-- src:1045 | main commencement date means the date on which section 10 of the Legislation (Repeals and Amendments) Act 2019 (which repeals the Legislation Act 2012) comes into force
#ASSERT `the main commencement date` (Date 1 1 2021) EQUALS Date 1 1 2021
-- src:1046 | publication commencement date means the date on which section 17 of the Legislation (Repeals and Amendments) Act 2019 comes into force (which brings into force the amendments requiring centralised publication as set out in Schedule 2 of the Legislation (Repeals and Amendments) Act 2019)
#ASSERT `the publication commencement date` (Date 1 6 2021) EQUALS Date 1 6 2021

§ `Schedule 1 clause 3 -- Part 2 of this Act applies to both existing and new legislation`

-- src:1053 | Part 2 of this Act applies to—
-- src:1054 | legislation whether it is enacted or made before, on, or after the main commencement date; and
-- src:1055 | anything that was an enactment under the Interpretation Act 1999 at the time it was made (or an amendment to that enactment made at any time).
#ASSERT `Part 2 applies to the legislation or enactment` TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Part 2 applies to the legislation or enactment` FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Part 2 applies to the legislation or enactment` FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

§ `Schedule 1 clause 4 -- Exception for examples in existing legislation`

-- src:1057 | 4 Exception for examples in existing legislation
-- src:1058 | Section 23 does not apply to an example provided in legislation that is enacted or made before the main commencement date (or an amendment, after that date, to that legislation).
-- src:1059 | This clause applies unless—
-- src:1060 | the legislation provides otherwise; or
-- src:1061 | the context of the legislation requires a different interpretation.
-- Arguments: day the legislation was enacted or made; the main commencement date; the example is in a later amendment; the legislation provides otherwise; the context requires otherwise.
-- Section 23 does not apply to an example in legislation enacted before 1 January 2021 ...
#ASSERT `section 23 applies to the example in legislation enacted or made on` (Date 31 12 2020) `given the main commencement date` (Date 1 1 2021) `where it is in a later amendment:` FALSE `and the legislation provides otherwise:` FALSE `or the context requires:` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- ... but does apply to an example in legislation enacted on the main commencement date, or after.
#ASSERT `section 23 applies to the example in legislation enacted or made on` (Date 1 1 2021) `given the main commencement date` (Date 1 1 2021) `where it is in a later amendment:` FALSE `and the legislation provides otherwise:` FALSE `or the context requires:` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `section 23 applies to the example in legislation enacted or made on` (Date 2 1 2021) `given the main commencement date` (Date 1 1 2021) `where it is in a later amendment:` FALSE `and the legislation provides otherwise:` FALSE `or the context requires:` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- An example in an amendment made after that date to old legislation is also outside section 23.
#ASSERT `section 23 applies to the example in legislation enacted or made on` (Date 5 5 2015) `given the main commencement date` (Date 1 1 2021) `where it is in a later amendment:` TRUE `and the legislation provides otherwise:` FALSE `or the context requires:` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Unless the legislation provides otherwise, or its context requires a different interpretation: then section 23 applies after all.
#ASSERT `section 23 applies to the example in legislation enacted or made on` (Date 5 5 2015) `given the main commencement date` (Date 1 1 2021) `where it is in a later amendment:` FALSE `and the legislation provides otherwise:` TRUE `or the context requires:` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `section 23 applies to the example in legislation enacted or made on` (Date 5 5 2015) `given the main commencement date` (Date 1 1 2021) `where it is in a later amendment:` FALSE `and the legislation provides otherwise:` FALSE `or the context requires:` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Together with section 23 itself (nz-part2-definitions.l4): an example in pre-commencement legislation does limit the provision, because section 23 does not apply and the text then says nothing.
#ASSERT `an example limits the provision` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Schedule 1 clause 5 -- Exception for commencement of secondary legislation made before main commencement date`

-- src:1063 | Section 26 does not apply to secondary legislation made before the main commencement date (and section 9 of the Interpretation Act 1999 applies instead).
#ASSERT `section 26 applies to secondary legislation made on` (Date 31 12 2020) `given the main commencement date` (Date 1 1 2021) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `section 26 applies to secondary legislation made on` (Date 1 1 2021) `given the main commencement date` (Date 1 1 2021) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `section 26 applies to secondary legislation made on` (Date 2 1 2021) `given the main commencement date` (Date 1 1 2021) EQUALS TRUE

§ `Schedule 1 clause 6 -- Saving of definitions for pre-1 November 1999 legislation`

-- src:1066 | In legislation enacted or made before 1 November 1999 (or an amendment, after that date, to that legislation),—
-- src:1067 | Act includes rules and regulations (within the meaning of those terms as used in the Acts Interpretation Act 1924) made under the Act
-- src:1068 | Governor means the Governor-General
-- src:1069 | land includes messuages, tenements, hereditaments, houses, and buildings unless there are words to exclude houses and buildings, or to restrict the meaning to tenements of some particular tenure
-- src:1070 | person includes a corporation sole, and also a body of persons, whether corporate or unincorporate.
-- src:1071 | This clause applies to legislation unless—
-- src:1072 | the legislation provides otherwise; or
-- src:1073 | the context of the legislation requires a different interpretation.
#ASSERT `the saved meaning of the term` Act `in legislation enacted or made on` (Date 31 10 1999) `when it is a later amendment:` FALSE `and it is displaced:` FALSE EQUALS JUST "includes rules and regulations (within the meaning of those terms as used in the Acts Interpretation Act 1924) made under the Act"
#ASSERT `the saved meaning of the term` Governor `in legislation enacted or made on` (Date 31 10 1999) `when it is a later amendment:` FALSE `and it is displaced:` FALSE EQUALS JUST "means the Governor-General"
#ASSERT `the saved meaning of the term` land `in legislation enacted or made on` (Date 3 3 1985) `when it is a later amendment:` FALSE `and it is displaced:` FALSE EQUALS JUST "includes messuages, tenements, hereditaments, houses, and buildings unless there are words to exclude houses and buildings, or to restrict the meaning to tenements of some particular tenure"
#ASSERT `the saved meaning of the term` person `in legislation enacted or made on` (Date 31 10 1999) `when it is a later amendment:` FALSE `and it is displaced:` FALSE EQUALS JUST "includes a corporation sole, and also a body of persons, whether corporate or unincorporate"
-- The day of 1 November 1999 itself is not before it.
#ASSERT `the saved meaning of the term` person `in legislation enacted or made on` (Date 1 11 1999) `when it is a later amendment:` FALSE `and it is displaced:` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the saved meaning of the term` person `in legislation enacted or made on` (Date 1 1 2005) `when it is a later amendment:` FALSE `and it is displaced:` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- An amendment made after 1 November 1999 to legislation enacted before it is covered; unless displaced.
#ASSERT `the saved meaning of the term` person `in legislation enacted or made on` (Date 1 1 1990) `when it is a later amendment:` TRUE `and it is displaced:` FALSE EQUALS JUST "includes a corporation sole, and also a body of persons, whether corporate or unincorporate"
#ASSERT `the saved meaning of the term` person `in legislation enacted or made on` (Date 1 1 1990) `when it is a later amendment:` FALSE `and it is displaced:` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the saved meaning of the term` `another term` `in legislation enacted or made on` (Date 1 1 1990) `when it is a later amendment:` FALSE `and it is displaced:` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Clause 6 saved meanings by member (ruling C): "Act includes", "land includes", "person includes" are open (off the list NOTHING); "Governor means" is closed (anyone else JUST FALSE).
-- src:1067 | Act includes rules and regulations (within the meaning of those terms as used in the Acts Interpretation Act 1924) made under the Act
-- src:1068 | Governor means the Governor-General
-- src:1069 | land includes messuages, tenements, hereditaments, houses, and buildings unless there are words to exclude houses and buildings, or to restrict the meaning to tenements of some particular tenure
-- src:1070 | person includes a corporation sole, and also a body of persons, whether corporate or unincorporate.
#ASSERT `is within the saved meaning of the pre-1 November 1999 term` `rules made under the Act` `unless there are words to exclude houses and buildings:` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `is within the saved meaning of the pre-1 November 1999 term` `regulations made under the Act` `unless there are words to exclude houses and buildings:` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `is within the saved meaning of the pre-1 November 1999 term` `the Governor-General` `unless there are words to exclude houses and buildings:` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `is within the saved meaning of the pre-1 November 1999 term` `someone other than the Governor-General` `unless there are words to exclude houses and buildings:` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `is within the saved meaning of the pre-1 November 1999 term` `messuages` `unless there are words to exclude houses and buildings:` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `is within the saved meaning of the pre-1 November 1999 term` `tenements` `unless there are words to exclude houses and buildings:` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `is within the saved meaning of the pre-1 November 1999 term` `hereditaments` `unless there are words to exclude houses and buildings:` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `is within the saved meaning of the pre-1 November 1999 term` `houses` `unless there are words to exclude houses and buildings:` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `is within the saved meaning of the pre-1 November 1999 term` `houses` `unless there are words to exclude houses and buildings:` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `is within the saved meaning of the pre-1 November 1999 term` `buildings` `unless there are words to exclude houses and buildings:` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `is within the saved meaning of the pre-1 November 1999 term` `buildings` `unless there are words to exclude houses and buildings:` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `is within the saved meaning of the pre-1 November 1999 term` `a corporation sole` `unless there are words to exclude houses and buildings:` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `is within the saved meaning of the pre-1 November 1999 term` `a body of persons that is corporate` `unless there are words to exclude houses and buildings:` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `is within the saved meaning of the pre-1 November 1999 term` `a body of persons that is unincorporate` `unless there are words to exclude houses and buildings:` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `is within the saved meaning of the pre-1 November 1999 term` `something else` `unless there are words to exclude houses and buildings:` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Schedule 1 clause 7 -- Saving of definitions for legislation made before main commencement date`

-- src:1075 | In legislation enacted or made before the main commencement date (or an amendment, after that date, to that legislation), regulations has the meaning set out in section 29 of the Interpretation Act 1999 (as in force immediately before that date).
-- src:1076 | This clause applies to legislation unless—
-- src:1077 | the legislation provides otherwise; or
-- src:1078 | the context of the legislation requires a different interpretation.
#ASSERT `regulations has the meaning in section 29 of the Interpretation Act 1999 for legislation enacted or made on` (Date 31 12 2020) `given the main commencement date` (Date 1 1 2021) `when it is a later amendment:` FALSE `and it is displaced:` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `regulations has the meaning in section 29 of the Interpretation Act 1999 for legislation enacted or made on` (Date 1 1 2021) `given the main commencement date` (Date 1 1 2021) `when it is a later amendment:` FALSE `and it is displaced:` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `regulations has the meaning in section 29 of the Interpretation Act 1999 for legislation enacted or made on` (Date 1 1 2020) `given the main commencement date` (Date 1 1 2021) `when it is a later amendment:` TRUE `and it is displaced:` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `regulations has the meaning in section 29 of the Interpretation Act 1999 for legislation enacted or made on` (Date 5 5 2021) `given the main commencement date` (Date 1 1 2021) `when it is a later amendment:` TRUE `and it is displaced:` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `regulations has the meaning in section 29 of the Interpretation Act 1999 for legislation enacted or made on` (Date 31 12 2020) `given the main commencement date` (Date 1 1 2021) `when it is a later amendment:` FALSE `and it is displaced:` TRUE EQUALS FALSE

§ `Schedule 1 clause 8 -- Savings of previous Proclamations`

-- src:1080 | A Proclamation published in the Gazette before the main commencement date continues to be a proclamation for the purposes of section 13.
#ASSERT `a previous Proclamation continues to be a proclamation for section 13` TRUE (Date 31 12 2020) `given the main commencement date` (Date 1 1 2021) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `a previous Proclamation continues to be a proclamation for section 13` TRUE (Date 1 1 2021) `given the main commencement date` (Date 1 1 2021) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `a previous Proclamation continues to be a proclamation for section 13` FALSE (Date 31 12 2020) `given the main commencement date` (Date 1 1 2021) EQUALS FALSE

§ `Schedule 1 clause 9 -- Savings of material incorporated by reference under Legislation Act 2012`

-- src:1082 | Material incorporated by reference under subpart 2 of Part 3 of the Legislation Act 2012 must be treated as if—
-- src:1083 | it were incorporated by reference under section 64 of this Act; and
-- src:1084 | any notice given under section 52(2) of the Legislation Act 2012 as to where the material is available for inspection and purchase is public notice as to where it is publicly available for the purposes of clause 2(a) of Schedule 2 of this Act.
#ASSERT `the material is treated as incorporated by reference under section 64` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the material is treated as incorporated by reference under section 64` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the old notice is public notice of where the material is publicly available` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the old notice is public notice of where the material is publicly available` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- src:1085 | The chief executive may make it publicly available in another way permitted by Schedule 2 of this Act if the chief executive gives public notice as required by clause 2 of that schedule.
#ASSERT `the chief executive may make the material publicly available in another way permitted by Schedule 2` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the chief executive may make the material publicly available in another way permitted by Schedule 2` FALSE EQUALS FALSE

§ `Schedule 1 clause 10 -- How Abolition of Provinces Act 1875 affects provincial legislation`

-- src:1087 | Section 26 of the Acts Interpretation Act 1908 as set out in Schedule 2 of the Acts Interpretation Act 1924 continues to apply despite its repeal.
#ASSERT `the section continues to apply despite its repeal` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the section continues to apply despite its repeal` FALSE EQUALS FALSE

§ `Schedule 1 clause 13 -- Definition of secondary legislation is effective on main commencement date for all legislation`

-- src:1116 | An instrument made before that date that is in force under a provision that empowers the making of secondary legislation, under the Royal prerogative, or under an identified empowering provision, becomes, on the main commencement date, secondary legislation.
-- src:1117 | Examples
-- src:1118 | An order is made under section 100 of an Act before the main commencement date.
-- src:1119 | On the main commencement date, an amendment is made to section 100 by the Secondary Legislation Act so that it states that orders made under it are secondary legislation.
-- src:1120 | The order is secondary legislation.
-- src:1121 | An order is made under section 120 of an Act after the main commencement date.
-- src:1122 | The Secondary Legislation Act has been passed, amending section 120. The amendment will result in section 120 stating that orders made under it are secondary legislation. However, the amendment has not yet come into force. Under subclause (3), section 120 is an identified empowering provision.
-- src:1123 | The order is secondary legislation.
-- src:1124 | In addition, section 120 may be changed, as an interim step before the full amendments come into force, so that it clearly states that orders made under it are secondary legislation (see subclauses (4) and (5)).
-- src:1125 | An order is made under section 90 of a repealed Act. Section 90 was replaced by the section 100 referred to above.
-- src:1126 | The order continues in force as if it were made under section 100 (see section 36 of this Act and section 20 of the Interpretation Act 1999).
-- src:1127 | The order is secondary legislation.
-- Example 1 (lines 1118-1120): an order made under section 100 of an Act before the main commencement date; section 100 is then amended to say its orders are secondary legislation: the order is secondary legislation, from the main commencement date.
#ASSERT `the day an instrument made on` (Date 1 6 2020) `becomes secondary legislation, given the main commencement date` (Date 1 1 2021) `when` TRUE EQUALS JUST (Date 1 1 2021)
#ASSERT `the day an instrument made on` (Date 1 6 2020) `becomes secondary legislation, given the main commencement date` (Date 1 1 2021) `when` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- An instrument made on or after the main commencement date does not "become" secondary legislation under this subclause: the ordinary definition governs.
#ASSERT `the day an instrument made on` (Date 1 1 2021) `becomes secondary legislation, given the main commencement date` (Date 1 1 2021) `when` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- src:1128 | For the purposes of this Act, a provision is an identified empowering provision if an amendment to the legislation (a secondary legislation amendment)—
-- src:1129 | has been passed or made that will result in the legislation stating that instruments under that provision are secondary legislation; but
-- src:1130 | that amendment is not yet in force.
-- Example 2 (lines 1121-1124): section 120 will state its orders are secondary legislation but the amendment is not yet in force: an identified empowering provision. Once in force, it is no longer "identified".
#ASSERT `is an identified empowering provision` TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `is an identified empowering provision` TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `is an identified empowering provision` FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- src:1113 | The definition of secondary legislation—
-- src:1114 | applies to an instrument regardless of whether it is made before, on, or after the main commencement date; and
-- src:1115 | extends to an instrument made under an identified empowering provision (see subclause (3)).
#ASSERT `the instrument is secondary legislation under clause 13` FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the instrument is secondary legislation under clause 13` TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the instrument is secondary legislation under clause 13` FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Example 3 (lines 1125-1127): an order made under section 90 of a repealed Act, replaced by section 100, continues in force as if made under section 100 (section 36 of this Act).
#ASSERT `legislation made under repealed legislation continues in force as if made under the other legislation` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- src:1135 | Subpart 2 of Part 3 applies to those changes as if they were changes referred to in section 87, except that, for the purposes of ensuring that the secondary legislation amendments (and any other related amendments relating to listing, notification, publication, or presentation) are effective despite those changes,—
-- src:1136 | those changes must be treated as being revoked immediately before those secondary legislation amendments (and related amendments) come into force; and
-- src:1137 | section 90 (which deals with when editorial changes usually take effect) does not apply.
#ASSERT `section 90 applies to the change` TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `section 90 applies to the change` FALSE EQUALS TRUE

§ `Schedule 1 clause 14 -- Existing requirements continued as applicable publication requirements on main commencement date`

-- src:1139 | This clause applies, for the purposes of section 74(1)﻿(a), to empowering provisions that are enacted before the main commencement date.
-- src:1140 | For the purposes of the applicable publication requirements under that paragraph (as in force on the main commencement date),—
-- src:1141 | the PCO may record and publish, as the applicable publication requirements for the empowering provision,—
-- src:1142 | the 1 or more requirements to publish, notify, or otherwise make available secondary legislation made under the empowering provision that applied under an Act, with the same or substantially the same effect, immediately before the main commencement date; and with
-- src:1143 | any exemptions or limits on those requirements; and with
-- src:1144 | any necessary modifications in light of other amendments made to the legislation on or after the main commencement date; and
#ASSERT `the PCO may record and publish the earlier requirements as the applicable publication requirements` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the PCO may record and publish the earlier requirements as the applicable publication requirements` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- src:1145 | the PCO must publish those applicable publication requirements, on the legislation website, by publishing either a link to the previous provision that set out that requirement or the record made under paragraph (a).
#ASSERT `the PCO has published the applicable publication requirements as clause 14 requires` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the PCO has published the applicable publication requirements as clause 14 requires` TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the PCO has published the applicable publication requirements as clause 14 requires` FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE

§ `Schedule 1 clause 15 -- Maker must lodge minimum legislative information before list deadline (if clause applies)`

-- src:1148 | This clause applies to secondary legislation on and after the publication commencement date if—
-- src:1149 | it is made before the list deadline; and
-- src:1150 | it is not already required to be published by the PCO under Part 3 before that list deadline.
-- Arguments: day asked about; day made; publication commencement date; list deadline; already required to be published. Publication commencement 1 June 2021; list deadline 1 June 2022 (supplied).
#ASSERT `clause 15 applies on` (Date 1 6 2021) `to secondary legislation made on` (Date 1 3 2021) `when the publication commencement date is` (Date 1 6 2021) `and the list deadline is` (Date 1 6 2022) `and it is already required to be published:` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `clause 15 applies on` (Date 31 5 2021) `to secondary legislation made on` (Date 1 3 2021) `when the publication commencement date is` (Date 1 6 2021) `and the list deadline is` (Date 1 6 2022) `and it is already required to be published:` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `clause 15 applies on` (Date 1 8 2021) `to secondary legislation made on` (Date 31 5 2022) `when the publication commencement date is` (Date 1 6 2021) `and the list deadline is` (Date 1 6 2022) `and it is already required to be published:` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `clause 15 applies on` (Date 1 8 2021) `to secondary legislation made on` (Date 1 6 2022) `when the publication commencement date is` (Date 1 6 2021) `and the list deadline is` (Date 1 6 2022) `and it is already required to be published:` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `clause 15 applies on` (Date 1 8 2021) `to secondary legislation made on` (Date 1 7 2021) `when the publication commencement date is` (Date 1 6 2021) `and the list deadline is` (Date 1 6 2022) `and it is already required to be published:` TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- src:1152 | a list exemption applies to the secondary legislation; and
-- "Until the list deadline": through the deadline day itself (Item 5).
#ASSERT `a list exemption applies on` (Date 31 5 2022) `when the list deadline is` (Date 1 6 2022) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `a list exemption applies on` (Date 1 6 2022) `when the list deadline is` (Date 1 6 2022) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `a list exemption applies on` (Date 2 6 2022) `when the list deadline is` (Date 1 6 2022) EQUALS FALSE
-- src:1157 | The maker must, before the list deadline, lodge the minimum legislative information for the secondary legislation with the PCO for publication in accordance with the regulations (unless the secondary legislation ceases to be in force before the list deadline).
-- "Before the list deadline": the last day to lodge is the day before (Item 6).
#ASSERT `the minimum legislative information is lodged in time on` (Date 31 5 2022) `when the list deadline is` (Date 1 6 2022) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the minimum legislative information is lodged in time on` (Date 1 6 2022) `when the list deadline is` (Date 1 6 2022) EQUALS FALSE
-- src:1153 | the maker must continue to comply with the applicable publication requirements (to the extent required by section 73, as in force immediately before the publication commencement date); but
-- src:1154 | those applicable publication requirements are treated as satisfied if—
-- src:1155 | the minimum legislative information for the secondary legislation is, with the agreement of the PCO, instead lodged with the PCO for publication; and
-- src:1156 | the maker complies with the minimum requirements for publication set by regulations made under this Act that are applicable (if any).
#ASSERT `the applicable publication requirements are treated as satisfied until the list deadline` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the applicable publication requirements are treated as satisfied until the list deadline` TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the applicable publication requirements are treated as satisfied until the list deadline` FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- src:1158 | The secondary legislation is revoked on a date specified in the regulations if—
-- src:1159 | its minimum legislative information is not lodged with the PCO for publication; and
-- src:1160 | it is of a class that is specified by the regulations as being revoked on that date.
#ASSERT `the day the secondary legislation is revoked for want of minimum legislative information` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 1 2023) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 1 2023)
#ASSERT `the day the secondary legislation is revoked for want of minimum legislative information` FALSE TRUE (Date 1 1 2023) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the day the secondary legislation is revoked for want of minimum legislative information` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 1 2023) EQUALS NOTHING
-- src:1161 | The list deadline for secondary legislation is—
-- src:1162 | the first anniversary of the publication commencement date (unless paragraph (b) or (c) applies); or
-- src:1163 | a deadline after the publication commencement date and no later than the fifth anniversary of the publication commencement date that is set by the regulations for the relevant class of secondary legislation; or
-- src:1164 | a deadline earlier than a deadline under paragraph (a) or (b) that is set by agreement between the maker and the Chief Parliamentary Counsel.
-- Publication commencement 1 June 2021; first anniversary 1 June 2022; fifth 1 June 2026 (supplied). Arguments: pcd; first anniversary; fifth anniversary; regulations' deadline; agreed deadline.
#ASSERT `the list deadline given the publication commencement date` (Date 1 6 2021) `and the first anniversary` (Date 1 6 2022) `and the fifth anniversary` (Date 1 6 2026) `and the regulations' deadline` NOTHING `and the agreed deadline` NOTHING EQUALS JUST (Date 1 6 2022)
