§ `Schedule 2 clause 3 -- What is required to make material publicly available`

-- src:1304 | A requirement to make material publicly available under this schedule is a requirement that—
-- src:1305 | the material is—
-- src:1306 | made available on (or via a link on) an Internet site maintained by or on behalf of the administering agency, free of charge, unless doing so would infringe copyright; or
-- src:1307 | in any other case, available for inspection, free of charge, at a place notified on an Internet site maintained by or on behalf of the administering agency; and
-- src:1308 | the material is available for purchase, at a reasonable cost, from a place notified on an Internet site maintained by or on behalf of the administering agency; and
-- src:1309 | if the material is not in an official New Zealand language, an accurate translation in an official New Zealand language of the material is also available as set out in paragraphs (a) and (b).
-- Arguments: on the agency's Internet site free of charge; doing so would infringe copyright; available for inspection free of charge at a notified place; available for purchase at a reasonable cost from a notified place; in an official NZ language; translation also available.
#ASSERT `the material is made publicly available as clause 3 requires` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the material is made publicly available as clause 3 requires` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the material is made publicly available as clause 3 requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the material is made publicly available as clause 3 requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the material is made publicly available as clause 3 requires` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the material is made publicly available as clause 3 requires` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the material is made publicly available as clause 3 requires` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- src:1309 | if the material is not in an official New Zealand language, an accurate translation in an official New Zealand language of the material is also available as set out in paragraphs (a) and (b).
-- "An official New Zealand language" is not defined in the Act: NOTHING for every language (fork F15).
#ASSERT `is an official New Zealand language` English EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `is an official New Zealand language` `te reo Māori` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `is an official New Zealand language` `New Zealand Sign Language` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `is an official New Zealand language` `another language` EQUALS NOTHING
