-- src:1320 | A failure to comply with this schedule does not invalidate secondary legislation that incorporates material by reference.
#ASSERT `a failure to comply with Schedule 2 invalidates the secondary legislation` TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `a failure to comply with Schedule 2 invalidates the secondary legislation` FALSE EQUALS FALSE

§ `Schedule 3 -- Exemptions from presentation or disallowance (the opening rule)`

-- src:1322 | A presentation or disallowance exemption applies to secondary legislation (or part of secondary legislation) under this schedule if—
-- src:1323 | it is made under an empowering provision to which that exemption applies in accordance with the tables below; and
-- src:1324 | any exemption ground is met (if specified in the tables for the exemption).
#ASSERT `a presentation or disallowance exemption applies under Schedule 3` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `a presentation or disallowance exemption applies under Schedule 3` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `a presentation or disallowance exemption applies under Schedule 3` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `a presentation or disallowance exemption applies under Schedule 3` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `a presentation or disallowance exemption applies under Schedule 3` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- src:1330 | Compliance is inappropriate for reasons of security.
-- src:1345 | Compliance would prejudice the national security interests of New Zealand.
-- src:1363 | If the FMA is satisfied on reasonable grounds that it is proper to defer compliance on the ground of commercial confidentiality.
-- src:1367 | The secondary legislation is bylaws made under the regulations for the purposes of section 49 of Ngā Rohe Moana o Ngā Hapū o Ngāti Porou Act 2019.
-- src:1380 | The relevant chief executive considers that compliance would result in 1 or more of the following:
-- src:1381 | disclosure of commercially sensitive information:
-- src:1382 | disclosure of a trade secret:
-- src:1383 | prejudice to New Zealand’s position in current or future negotiations for overseas market access:
-- src:1384 | prejudice to the international relations of New Zealand.
-- src:1405 | The Takeovers Panel is satisfied on reasonable grounds that it is proper to defer compliance for reasons of commercial confidentiality.
-- src:1406 | Exemption applies while exemption ground is met
#ASSERT `the exemption ground is met in the way the deposited text shows` `Compliance is inappropriate for reasons of security` `when` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the exemption ground is met in the way the deposited text shows` `Compliance is inappropriate for reasons of security` `when` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the exemption ground is met in the way the deposited text shows` `Compliance would prejudice the national security interests of New Zealand` `when` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the exemption ground is met in the way the deposited text shows` `Compliance would prejudice the national security interests of New Zealand` `when` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the exemption ground is met in the way the deposited text shows` `The FMA is satisfied on reasonable grounds that it is proper to defer compliance on the ground of commercial confidentiality` `when` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the exemption ground is met in the way the deposited text shows` `The FMA is satisfied on reasonable grounds that it is proper to defer compliance on the ground of commercial confidentiality` `when` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the exemption ground is met in the way the deposited text shows` `The Takeovers Panel is satisfied on reasonable grounds that it is proper to defer compliance for reasons of commercial confidentiality` `when` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the exemption ground is met in the way the deposited text shows` `The Takeovers Panel is satisfied on reasonable grounds that it is proper to defer compliance for reasons of commercial confidentiality` `when` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the exemption ground is met in the way the deposited text shows` `The relevant chief executive considers that compliance would result in disclosure of commercially sensitive information, disclosure of a trade secret, prejudice to New Zealand's position in negotiations for overseas market access, or prejudice to the international relations of New Zealand` `when` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the exemption ground is met in the way the deposited text shows` `The relevant chief executive considers that compliance would result in disclosure of commercially sensitive information, disclosure of a trade secret, prejudice to New Zealand's position in negotiations for overseas market access, or prejudice to the international relations of New Zealand` `when` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- The four limbs of the chief executive's ground ("1 or more of the following"): each is met when the chief executive considers compliance would have that result (ruling C).
#ASSERT `the exemption ground is met in the way the deposited text shows` `The relevant chief executive considers that compliance would result in disclosure of commercially sensitive information` `when` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the exemption ground is met in the way the deposited text shows` `The relevant chief executive considers that compliance would result in disclosure of commercially sensitive information` `when` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the exemption ground is met in the way the deposited text shows` `The relevant chief executive considers that compliance would result in disclosure of a trade secret` `when` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
